From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:47:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Coroutine kernel groundwork: co_switch, 66 MiB arena,
 execution layer

- psprecomp::Coroutine: hand-written context switch for x86-64 SysV and
  ARMv7 AAPCS hard-float (r4-r11, lr, d8-d15, FPSCR), guard page and canary,
  high-water measurement; unit test.
- GuestMemory is backed by one 66 MiB arena (ARCHITECTURE.md 1): RAM at
  arena 0, scratchpad at 0x00010000, VRAM at 0x04000000; checked accessors
  keep mirror folding; g_ram published by the Runtime's memory.
- exec layer: g_cpu (the one register file), pk_guest_call / pk_hle_call /
  pk_fatal / pk_yield, weak g_lean_entry table, INTERP_ONLY / LEAN_ONLY,
  per-address kind table (native hook, lean entry, interpret).
- Interpreter: interpret_guest_call keeps interpreting across jal, calls
  import stubs and hooks directly, calls lean entries; optional histogram of
  loads/stores by 1 MiB region with the PCs of odd accesses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

